# BE3b exception: the pinned live-engine wheel and the runtime-bundle JSON Schema are governed
# runtime dependencies and must be resolvable in the build context. Only these exact files are
# allowed back in — the prohibited full research wheel (upadya-component-b-generator) and the
# rest of provenance/ (baseline manifests, closure decisions, generator source lock) stay
# excluded from the image.
!provenance/wheels/
provenance/wheels/*
!provenance/wheels/upadya_component_b_live_engine-0.1.0+be3.0e86fdc-py3-none-any.whl
# BF-4: re-pinned wheel. The BE3 line above is kept, not replaced — it is what lets the old,
# still-retained wheel be rebuilt into an image for historical verification if anyone ever needs
# to reproduce the BE3-era manifest entry; it is never installed today (nothing in
# requirements.lock references it) so keeping it in the build context is inert.
!provenance/wheels/upadya_component_b_live_engine-0.1.0+bf4.09267ab-py3-none-any.whl
!provenance/runtime-bundle.schema.json
# BE3c exception: the implemented/deferred template partition provenance is read by the
# characterization test suite to cross-check the TEST-FIXTURE-ONLY catalogue against the
# reviewed coverage report. Contains no generator source, no wheel, no research artifacts.
!provenance/component-b-coverage.json
